      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-6017",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=-0.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =2\\cdot (-0.5)+\u230a\\frac{-0.5}{5}\u230b \\\\  & =-1+\u230a-0.1\u230b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u230a-0.1\u230b=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.5) & =-1+\u230a-0.1\u230b \\\\  & =-1+(-1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036384/example-6017.json",
          "file_sha256": "a3ba86545055ba10e390e932d70cf4a963ee5f6eb19cb2ead2ab3fab523a631b"
