          "question": "e-13202",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lfloor x \\rfloor = n,\n\\quad\\text{where}\\quad\nn \\leq x \\lt n+1,\\quad  n\\in \\mathbb Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x = 0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{\u230a0.75+2\u230b}}{2(0.75)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\u230a2.75\u230b}}{2.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\left\\lfloor 2.75\\right\\rfloor = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =\\frac{{e}^{\u230a2.75\u230b}}{2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2.5} \\\\  & =2.955\\,62\u2026 \\\\  & \u22482.96,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
